# 64 GB tier, night 64-3: the hybrid arm (plan.md §5.1 suite 3, §5.3). Sonnet 5 orchestrates
# through nav-pilot and opencode; a local worker takes the dispatched subtasks.
# NOT READY (pilot, 2026-09-27, pending-tasks §8.8): nav-pilot-main-dd859ac6 refuses a launch
# without a terminal unless given --sync, and --sync rewrites the user's ~/.copilot agents, so
# neither bench-hybrid's samples nor night-run-3's cloud gate can run on it; and Sonnet 5 did not
# dispatch on tasks:3 in the pilot (0 of 2). Resolve both before this queue runs.
# Before: mise run vram-set 48 (every profile here declares 48).
# Run (the cap covers every sample, invalid ones included; the cloud probes, ~$0.05 each, ~$0.70 a night, are outside it):
#   FRONTIER_COST_CAP=35 BENCH_NAV_PILOT=/Users/hans/mlx-workspace/.bench-logs/bin/nav-pilot-main-dd859ac6 \
#     mise run night-run-3 -- --part hybrid --queue reports/2026-09-26-64gb-tier/night-64-3.queue
#
# Files are tagged np-dd859ac6-sonnet5; bench-hybrid adds the worker profile to each hybrid
# file's name, so the three workers are three populations. The control arm dispatches nothing
# (`alpha local off`), runs once per cell under optiq-64g's server, and serves all three.
#
# The trusted cell is three (target, rung) cells, not four: tasks:6 is D2, retired in
# bench/tasks.json, so bench-hybrid refuses it. edit-multi's D2 evidence is spring-ia:6 alone.
# Order is by cell, so a night cut short by the cap or the clock still has complete
# control-against-worker comparisons for the cells it reached.
#
# Workers: optiq-64g is the control worker (the manifest's own entry and its capabilities);
# 8-bit and Occamy get a bench entry with no capabilities block (nav-pilot's unmeasured policy
# text), never optiq's verdicts. policy.sha256 is recorded per sample.
# Laguna is left out: nav-pilot's mlx-lm 0.31.3 has no `laguna`.
#
# Timeouts: one step is one (cell, arm, worker), 8 valid samples. Expected ~3 min a sample
# (copilot-mixed-mode research §3.2: ~3.2 h per 64) plus a server start. 120 min covers 8
# samples at up to ~14 min each, or a few invalid retries; it does not cover bench-hybrid's
# worst case (18 attempts at a 900 s cap, 270 min). A step cut at 120 min keeps what it
# recorded and resumes to 8 valid samples on a rerun of that line.
# The cloud probe runs before each step (~$0.05, outside the cap), not during one.
#
# part  kind   target                        arm     samples rung timeout expected profile
hybrid hybrid tasks                         control 8 3 120 30 qwen3.6-35b-a3b-optiq-64g
hybrid hybrid tasks                         hybrid  8 3 120 30 qwen3.6-35b-a3b-optiq-64g
hybrid hybrid tasks                         hybrid  8 3 120 40 qwen3.6-35b-a3b-8bit-64g
hybrid hybrid tasks                         hybrid  8 3 120 30 occamy-1.0-4bit-64g
